W:A-A-B-A, up-tempo with the B in swing.
W:Drums tick (ride/hi-hat).
W:B is the bridge.
W:2nd trumpet: harmony notes, and long notes under the bridge.
W:Trombone fills in; sousaphone, washboard and banjos hold the rhythm tight and are the engine of the tune.
W:Riff = Kees Tijssen 5, first part as written by Kees Tijssen. Riff under all the A's; under the B long notes are played.
